{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"command -v clojure java bb && rg --files .cpcache | head -20 && sed -n '1,110p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj && cat collab/yang-clojure/1793955600000-engineer-h3-6-audit-fixes.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/clojure/1.12.4.1602/bin/clojure\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/java/21.0.2/bin/java\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/babashka/1.13.225/bb\n.cpcache/532883802.main\n.cpcache/4155935546.main\n.cpcache/3640668897.cp\n.cpcache/1237327589.manifest\n.cpcache/1875258622.main\n.cpcache/3296283869.basis\n.cpcache/3246607206.manifest\n.cpcache/1237327589.cp\n.cpcache/2127443215.cp\n.cpcache/350423856.cp\n.cpcache/4093444987.cp\n.cpcache/3246607206.main\n.cpcache/2224835971.cp\n.cpcache/4207610051.cp\n.cpcache/4183786633.manifest\n.cpcache/2171153092.cp\n.cpcache/3625694803.basis\n.cpcache/2127443215.basis\n.cpcache/4155935546.cp\n.cpcache/2453741936.basis\n(ns yang.latte-oracle-test\n  \"Pinned upstream LaTTe differential harness, slices 1-9 of the Yang gap\n   program. A executes the original library on Clojure. B executes explicit\n   portability source on Clojure; C compiles it through Yang for the walker\n   and semantic VMs. Slice 9 fails closed on the full kernel corpus. The\n   legacy classifier records historical blockers;\n   the context module additionally checks free-symbol admission before C.\n   Adaptations, operation sequences and scope departures live beside the\n   manifest in yang/latte_oracle/.\"\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [clojure.tools.reader :as r]\n            [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as rows-support]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n\n\n(def ^:private manifest\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn- ns-declaration-aliases\n  \"Alias -> full ns symbol, taken from the file's own (ns ...) declaration —\n   never invented: ::alias/kw must read as :that.real.ns/kw.\"\n  [ns-form]\n  (let [alias-map (atom {})\n        consume-spec (fn [spec]\n                       (when (sequential? spec)\n                         (let [lib (first spec)]\n                           (loop [xs (rest spec)]\n                             (when (seq xs)\n                               (if (= :as (first xs))\n                                 (do (swap! alias-map assoc (second xs) lib)\n                                     (recur (drop 2 xs)))\n                                 (recur (next xs))))))))]\n    (loop [clauses (rest (rest ns-form))]\n      (when (seq clauses)\n        (let [clause (first clauses)]\n          (if (and (seq? clause) (= :require (first clause)))\n            (do (loop [reqs (next clause)]\n                  (let [spec (first reqs)]\n                    (when (and (not (nil? spec)) (not (keyword? spec)))\n                      (consume-spec spec)\n                      (recur (next reqs)))))\n                (recur (next clauses)))\n            (recur (next clauses))))))\n    @alias-map))\n\n\n(defn- read-forms\n  \"Read one latte-kernel source file with reader conditionals resolved for\n   :clj, ::alias/kw keywords resolved against the file's own ns declaration,\n   and ::kw resolved against the file's own namespace — so the C leg compiles\n   the same keyword identities the upstream A leg runs.\"\n  [ns-sym]\n  (let [f (io/resource (str (str/replace (name ns-sym) \".\" \"/\") \".cljc\"))\n        pr (rt/source-logging-push-back-reader (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader f)) 1 (str f))\n        ns-form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)\n        declared-name (second ns-form)\n        aliases (ns-declaration-aliases ns-form)]\n    (binding [r/*alias-map* aliases\n              *ns* (the-ns (create-ns declared-name))]\n      (loop [acc []]\n        (let [form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)]\n          (if (= form ::eof) acc (recur (conj acc form))))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private all-forms\n  (into {} (map (fn [ns-sym] [ns-sym (read-forms ns-sym)])\n                (distinct (map :ns manifest)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private top-forms\n  (into {} (map (fn [{:keys [ns kind name]}]\n                  [[ns name] (first (filter #(and (seq? %)\n                                                  (= kind (first %))\n                                                  (= name (second %)))\n                                            (get all-forms ns)))]))\n        manifest))\n\n\n(def ^:private scanned-symbols\n  #{'loop 'recur 'case 'throw 'ex-info 'atom 'swap! 'reset! 'lazy-seq 'gensym\n    'apply 'comp 'partial 'reduced 'reduce 'map 'mapv 'filter 'remove 'into\n    'concat 'merge 'str 'symbol 'keyword 'vector 'seq 'nth 'nthnext 'assoc-in\n    'count 'name 'when-let 'if-let 'when-some 'if-some 'cond})\n\n\n(defn- walk-symbols\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (seq? form) (if (and (= 'quote (first form)) (= 2 (count form)))\n                  #{}\n                  (mapcat walk-symbols form))\nFixed both findings in [latte_oracle_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2404). [Applied diff](/private/tmp/yang-oracle-audit-fix/fix.patch).\n\n- Hashing now renames generated symbols by first occurrence across `[forms call]`, preserving shared references. Regression tests cover repeated NBE reads, symbol identity, and ordinary source changes.\n- Case 6 uses `:nbe-beta`, requires a dynamic site executed in both lanes, and runs the refusal assertion unconditionally.\n\nVerification passed:\n\n- **5 tests, 1,393 assertions; zero failures/errors.**\n- Fresh JVM with advanced reader counter: **155/155 hashes identical**, **165/165 arities credited**.\n- All **20,805 site rows unchanged**; 60 hashes normalized.\n- Lint: zero errors, two existing warnings. Whitespace check passed.\n\nOnly the requested source file changed. Artifacts were regenerated in a temporary directory. To refresh the committed EDN files:\n\n```sh\nclojure -Sdeps \\\n  '{:aliases {:refresh {:main-opts [\"-e\" \"(require (quote yang.latte-oracle-test)) (yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!)\"]}}}' \\\n  -M:test:refresh\n```","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
